 "drivingQuestion": "Corresponding to what did David say the fifteen Songs of Ascents?",
 "outcome": "inconclusive",
 "outcomeNote": "The difficulty is answered in the next unit (sukkah.sugya207) by Rav Ḥisda's corrected version.",
 "continuesQuestionOf": null,
 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "sukkah.53a.12",
   "daf": "53a",
   "sentenceId": 11,
   "he": "חֲמֵשׁ עֶשְׂרֵה מַעֲלוֹת. אֲמַר לֵיהּ רַב חִסְדָּא לְהָהוּא מִדְּרַבָּנַן דַּהֲוָה קָמְסַדַּר אַגָּדָתָא קַמֵּיהּ, אֲמַר לֵיהּ: שְׁמִיעַ לְךָ, הָנֵי חֲמֵשׁ עֶשְׂרֵה מַעֲלוֹת, כְּנֶגֶד מִי אֲמָרָם דָּוִד? אֲמַר לֵיהּ: הָכִי אָמַר רַבִּי יוֹחָנָן: בְּשָׁעָה שֶׁכָּרָה דָּוִד שִׁיתִין, קְפָא תְּהוֹמָא וּבָעֵי לְמִשְׁטְפֵיהּ לְעָלְמָא. אָמַר דָּוִד חֲמֵשׁ עֶשְׂרֵה מַעֲלוֹת וְהוֹרִידָן. אִי הָכִי, חֲמֵשׁ עֶשְׂרֵה ״מַעֲלוֹת״ — ״יוֹרְדוֹת״ מִיבְּעֵי לֵיהּ!",
   "en": "§ The mishna continues: The musicians would stand on the «fifteen stairs» that descend from the Israelites’ courtyard to the Women’s Courtyard, corresponding to the fifteen Songs of the Ascents in Psalms. «Rav Ḥisda said to one of the Sages who was organizing aggada before him: Did you hear» with regard to «these fifteen» Songs of «Ascents» in Psalms, «corresponding to what did David say them? He said to him» that «this» is what «Rabbi Yoḥanan said: At the time that David dug the drainpipes» in the foundation of the Temple, the waters of «the depths rose and sought to inundate the world.» Immediately, «David recited the fifteen» Songs of the «Ascents and caused them to subside.» Rav Ḥisda asked: «If so,» should they be called «fifteen» Songs of the «Ascents? They should have been» called Songs of the «Descents.»"
  }
 ],
